<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ title }} — manuscriptor</title>
  <style>{{ styles_css | safe }}</style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="topbar-row">
      <h1 class="doc-title">{{ title }}</h1>
      <div class="topbar-stats">
        <span class="stat">{{ n_pairs }} cite-instances</span>
        <span class="badge badge-verbatim">{{ n_verbatim }} verbatim</span>
        <span class="badge badge-paraphrase">{{ n_paraphrase }} paraphrase</span>
        <span class="badge badge-missing">{{ n_missing }} missing</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="topbar-row">
      <input type="search" id="filter-input" placeholder="Filter citations by key, author, or title…" autocomplete="off">
      <div class="topbar-meta">
        <span>{{ generated_at }}</span>
        <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
        <a href="#about-tool">about this tool</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="split">
    <article class="manuscript" id="manuscript">
      {{ manuscript_html | safe }}

      <section id="about-tool" class="about">
        <h2>About this view</h2>
        <p>
          Each citation in this manuscript is linked to verbatim quotes extracted from
          the cited paper's fulltext. Click any citation to open the evidence panel.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><span class="badge badge-verbatim">verbatim</span> the quoted passage is an exact substring of the cited paper.</li>
          <li><span class="badge badge-paraphrase">paraphrase</span> the model reported a supporting passage, but the exact text could not be matched in the cited paper. Treat with care.</li>
          <li><span class="badge badge-missing">missing</span> no supporting passage was found, or the cited paper has no indexed fulltext in the local library.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="caveat">
          This is a review aid. The verbatim check catches hallucinated quotes but does not
          guarantee that a verbatim quote is used in a context that supports the claim.
          Read the cited paper before relying on any claim flagged here.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <aside class="panel" id="evidence-panel">
      <div class="panel-placeholder">
        <p>Click any citation in the manuscript to see the supporting evidence.</p>
        <p class="hint">Citation borders show the strongest evidence status across the cited papers.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </main>

  <script>
    window.CITE_EVIDENCE = {
      title: {{ title_json | safe }},
      claims: {{ claims_json | safe }},
      citations_by_key: {{ citations_by_key_json | safe }},
      evidence_by_pair: {{ evidence_by_pair_json | safe }}
    };
  </script>
  <script>{{ viewer_js | safe }}</script>
</body>
</html>
